  "intro": {
    "en": "Today we go out into the street. \"Just a pigeon\", \"just a crow\": that's what most people say. But walk through any British town and you'll find three kinds of pigeon and three kinds of crow, often on the same roof.\n\nFor each bird you learn the one detail that gives it away: a white patch on the neck, a black collar, a pale eye. Once you've seen it, you won't mix them up again.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of ten questions, with birds from the first two lessons mixed in."
  },
  "words": [
